```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "tracker": {
      "type": "http",
      "url": "https://mcp.tracker.example.com/mcp",
      "headers": { "Authorization": "Bearer trk_live_9f2c41d8e7" }
    }
  }
}
```

What should you do before committing it?

Scenario: Customer Support Resolution Agent. A nightly CI job runs `claude -p` to regression-test the support agent's prompts against the order-lookup MCP server defined in the repository's .mcp.json. The job exits 0, but every transcript shows the agent answering without ever calling an order tool.

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "orders": {
      "url": "https://mcp.shop.example.com/orders",
      "headers": { "Authorization": "Bearer ${ORDERS_TOKEN}" }
    }
  }
}
```

What is the cause, and what is the right safeguard?

